{
  "about": [
    "Technical names and technical verbs of the Apsis project that are not glossary entries. The tool tools/ste/ste-lint.mjs reads this file.",
    "THIS IS A PROJECT LIST. The official ASD-STE100 specification and its dictionary were not available.",
    "ASD-STE100 lets a writer use a word that is not in the dictionary if the word is a technical name (rule 1.5) or a technical verb (rule 1.12). Each group below has the category that the author thinks is applicable. The category texts are from the memory of the author (ASD-STE100, issue 7). No person compared them with the specification.",
    "The terms of orbital mechanics are not in this file. They are in the glossary (src/i18n/locales/en/90-glossary.json): the tool reads each glossary term as a technical name, and each glossary entry with a definition that starts with 'To ' as a technical verb. Most glossary terms are of the category 'science'. Some are names of organizations, of documents or of services. The definition in the glossary is the record for each term.",
    "names: 'case' = the tool compares capital letters and small letters (symbols, units, abbreviations in which the capital letters are important). 'plural: false' = the name has no plural. 'pos: adj' = the name is an adjective. An item can be a text or an object { name, plural, see }. 'see' is the id of the glossary entry that gives the definition of a related name.",
    "kind 'symbol': characters that are not letters. kind 'extension': the last part of a file name (the tool reads a text of the form name.ext as a file name).",
    "patterns: regular expressions for identifiers that have a constant form (versions, document numbers, keywords of file formats).",
    "verbs: 'forms' = third person, past, past participle. 'noun: true' = the noun has the same form (example: a search)."
  ],
  "categories": {
